From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000008 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Omer Faruk Nehir <omerfaruknehir@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 00:58:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] i2c: qcom-cci: fail closed on hold restore error

The platform clock-hold API changes the CCI functional clock only while normal
I2C transfers are excluded. Do not reopen transfers if restoring the pre-hold
rate fails or returns a different rate.

Latch a fault in that case. A faulted controller rejects both new platform
holds and normal I2C transfers, leaving recovery to an explicit unbind/reboot
instead of operating with uncertain timing. Runtime PM may still suspend the
idle hardware after the failed restore; the fault gate prevents a later resume
from being used for transfers.

This remains compile-only plumbing: no caller is added by this patch.

Signed-off-by: Omer Faruk Nehir <omerfaruknehir@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c | 16 +++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c
index 000000000001..000000000002 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c
@@ -152,6 +152,7 @@ struct cci {
 	unsigned long platform_hold_restore_rate;
 	unsigned int platform_hold_count;
 	unsigned int platform_active_xfers;
+	bool platform_hold_faulted;
 };
 
 static irqreturn_t cci_isr(int irq, void *dev)
@@ -437,7 +438,7 @@ static int cci_platform_xfer_get(struct cci *cci)
 	int ret = 0;
 
 	mutex_lock(&cci->platform_hold_lock);
-	if (cci->platform_hold_count)
+	if (cci->platform_hold_count || cci->platform_hold_faulted)
 		ret = -EBUSY;
 	else
 		cci->platform_active_xfers++;
@@ -477,6 +478,11 @@ int qcom_cci_platform_hold_get(struct device *dev, unsigned long rate)
 
 	mutex_lock(&cci->platform_hold_lock);
 
+	if (cci->platform_hold_faulted) {
+		ret = -EIO;
+		goto out_unlock;
+	}
+
 	if (!cci->platform_hold_clk) {
 		ret = -ENODEV;
 		goto out_unlock;
@@ -544,10 +550,12 @@ err_restore:
 	actual_rate = clk_get_rate(cci->platform_hold_clk);
 	if (!restore_ret && actual_rate != restore_rate)
 		restore_ret = -ERANGE;
-	if (restore_ret)
+	if (restore_ret) {
+		cci->platform_hold_faulted = true;
 		dev_err(dev,
 			"failed to restore CCI clock after platform hold error: %d\n",
 			restore_ret);
+	}
 err_pm_put:
 	pm_runtime_mark_last_busy(dev);
 	pm_runtime_put_autosuspend(dev);
@@ -591,10 +599,12 @@ int qcom_cci_platform_hold_put(struct device *dev)
 	if (!ret && actual_rate != restore_rate)
 		ret = -ERANGE;
-	if (ret)
+	if (ret) {
+		cci->platform_hold_faulted = true;
 		dev_err(dev, "failed to restore CCI platform-hold rate: %d\n", ret);
-
-	cci->platform_hold_rate = 0;
-	cci->platform_hold_restore_rate = 0;
+	} else {
+		cci->platform_hold_rate = 0;
+		cci->platform_hold_restore_rate = 0;
+	}
 	pm_runtime_mark_last_busy(dev);
 	pm_runtime_put_autosuspend(dev);
 
